        "Basis", "`mat4` (`rotation_y(a)`, `look_at`) or a quaternion (vec4)",
        "Transform3D", "`mat4` (`translation(p) * rotation_y(a)`)",
        "Quaternion", "`quat_euler(pitch, yaw, roll)` or `quat_axis_angle(axis, angle)` (a quaternion is a vec4), or a matrix: `rotation_y(45deg)`",
        "lerp_angle", "`approach_angle` or `turn_toward`",
        "free", "nothing: memory is given back when the last use of it is gone",
        "malloc", "an array (`fill(u8(0), n)`, given back by itself)",
        "memcpy", "`mem_copy(dst, src, n)`",
        "memmove", "`mem_copy(dst, src, n)`",
        "memset", "`fill(u8(0), n)` for a new array, or a loop",
        "tostring", "`str(x)`",
        "tonumber", "`to_int(s)` or `to_float(s)` (an optional: none when it is not a number)",
        "ipairs", "`loop i in 0.. and x in xs:`",
        "pairs", "`loop k, v in m:`",
        "math", "the plain functions: `floor(x)`, `sqrt(x)`, `random()`",
        "table", "an array (`T[]`) or a map (`\{K: V}`)",
        "require", "`import name` (a library module) or `use 'file.jo'`",
        "set", "a map to `bool` (`\{str: bool}`) or `unique(xs)`",
        "Set", "a map to `bool` (`\{str: bool}`) or `unique(xs)`",
        "every", "`all(xs, f)`",
        "some", "`any(xs, f)`",
        "at", "`xs[i]` (the last: `xs[end]`)",
        "slice", "a slice: `xs[a..b)`",
        "concat", "`xs + ys`",
        "splice", "`xs.insert(i, x)` or `xs.remove(i)`",
        "shift", "`xs.remove(0)`",
        "unshift", "`xs.insert(0, x)`",
        "flatMap", "`flatten(map(xs, f))`",
        "flat_map", "`flatten(map(xs, f))`",
        "findIndex", "`find_index(xs, f)`",
        "toFixed", "\"\{x:.2}\" (two decimals)",
        "reverse", "`reversed(xs)`",
        "Mathf", "the plain functions: `clamp(x, lo, hi)`, `lerp(a, b, t)`, `sin(x)`, `abs(x)`, `PI`",
        "Debug", "`print(x)`",
        "GameObject", "`struct Enemy:` for each kind of thing, kept in an array (`enemies: Enemy[]`; docs/START.md, Coming from Unity)",
        "SceneManager", "an enum saying which screen or level is on (`screen = .play`), and a function that sets one up",
        "Physics", "`import physics3d` (2D: `import physics`), then `w = physics3d.World()` and `w.raycast(a, b)`",
        "Rigidbody", "`import physics3d`, then a body of its world: `ball = w.add_sphere(pos, 0.5)`",
        "Instantiate", "`enemies.push(make_enemy(pos))`, with a function of yours that makes the struct",
        "Destroy", "`enemies.remove(i)` (taking it out of its array), or `enemies.retain((e): e.hp > 0)`",
        "GetComponent", "the field itself, `player.health` (there are no components: a struct holds what it has)",
        "Collision", "`w.contacts(b)`, read each frame (`c.new`: it just began); nothing is called when bodies touch",
        "Time", "the `dt` update is given (the seconds since the last frame), or `time()` (since the start)",
        "wait", "a timer counted down in update (`wait -= dt`, then act when it is below 0), `every(1, 2.0)`, or `Actions`: `steps.then(1.0, (): ...)`",
        "create_clone", "a list of things: `apples.push(Apple(pos))` makes one more (Scratch's clones)",
        "clone", "a list of things: `apples.push(Apple(pos))` makes one more (Scratch's clones)",
        "delete_this_clone", "mark it in its loop (`a.gone = true`), then `apples.retain((a): not a.gone)`",
        "broadcast", "a function of your own, called where the message is sent: `level_up()`",
        "switch_costume", "a variable saying which picture to draw (`costume = 1`), and `sprite(costumes[costume], pos)` in draw",
        "next_costume", "a variable saying which picture to draw (`costume = (costume + 1) % costumes.len()`)",
        "go_to", "`pos = vec2(100, 200)` (the position is a variable)",
        "goto", "`pos = vec2(100, 200)` (the position is a variable)",
        "hide", "a variable saying whether it shows (`shown = false`), and `if shown:` around its drawing",
        "show", "a variable saying whether it shows (`shown = true`), and `if shown:` around its drawing",
        "touching", "`overlaps(Rect(...), Rect(...))` or `circles_overlap(a, 20, b, 20)`",
        "pick_random", "`random_int(1, 11)` (1 to 10: the top is left out)",
        "say", "`text(\"Hello!\", pos + vec2(30, -40))` in draw, while a timer for it is running",
        "think", "`text(\"Hmm...\", pos + vec2(30, -40))` in draw, while a timer for it is running",
        "glide", "`move = tween(pos, vec2(600, 300), 1.0)`, then `move.update(dt)` and `pos = move.value()` each frame",
        "stop_all", "`quit()`",
        "when_flag_clicked", "nothing: the lines at the top of the file run first, once",
        "Add", "`push`",
        "Remove", "`remove(i)` (by position)",
        "Insert", "`insert(i, x)`",
        "Contains", "`contains`",
        "Clear", "`clear`",
        "IndexOf", "`index_of`",
        "Counter", "`counts: \{str: int} = \{}`, then `counts[w] += 1` (a map: a missing key starts at 0)",
        "defaultdict", "a plain map: a missing key starts at its type's zero (`m[k] += 1`, `m[k].push(x)`)",
        "open", "`read_file(path)` (a `str?`: none when it cannot be read), `write_file(path, s)`, `append_file(path, s)`",
        "sys", "`args()` (the command line), `exit(code)`, `eprint(s)`",
        "isinstance", "`x is T` (which member of a union x holds)",
        "index", "`index_of`",
        "isdigit", "`to_int(s) != none`, or `is_digit(c)` for one character",
        "partition", "`split(s, \"=\", 1)` (at most two parts)",
        "splitlines", "`lines(s)`",
        "loads", "`parse_json(s)` (a Json), or `from_json[T](s)` into a struct",
        "dumps", "`to_json(x)`",
        "json", "`parse_json(s)` and `to_json(x)` (there, without an import)",
        "os", "the plain functions: `read_file`, `list_dir`, `join_path`, `run_program`, `env`",
        "normalized", "`normalize(v)`",
        "magnitude", "`length(v)`",
        "sqrMagnitude", "`length_sq(v)`",
        "TWO_PI", "`TAU`",
        "HALF_PI", "`PI / 2.0`",
        "QUARTER_PI", "`PI / 4.0`",
        "width", "`screen_width()` (the screen's, in 2D units)",
        "height", "`screen_height()` (the screen's, in 2D units)",
        "color", "`rgb(1, 0, 0)` (each from 0 to 1) or `hex(0xff0000)`",
        "stroke", "the color given to each shape: `line(a, b, 2, RED)`, `ring(center, radius, 2, RED)`",
        "strokeWeight", "the thickness given to each shape: `line(a, b, 4, c)`, `ring(center, radius, 4, c)`",
        "noStroke", "nothing: a shape has no outline unless drawn with one (`rect_outline`, `ring`)",
        "noFill", "an outline: `rect_outline`, `ring`, `polyline(points, width, c, closed = true)`",
        "background", "`clear(color)` at the top of draw",
        "createCanvas", "`window(\"title\", w, h)` at the top of the file",
        "size", "`window(\"title\", w, h)`",
        "mouseX", "`mouse_pos().x`",
        "mouseY", "`mouse_pos().y`",
        "pmouseX", "`(mouse_pos() - mouse_delta()).x`",
        "pmouseY", "`(mouse_pos() - mouse_delta()).y`",
        "mouseIsPressed", "`mouse_down(.left)` (held) or `mouse_pressed(.left)` (just pressed)",
        "keyIsPressed", "`key_down(.space)` for a key, `text_input()` for what was typed",
        "keyIsDown", "`key_down(.a)`",
